; The .home zone as install.sh first writes it: the zone's own records and
; nothing else. After that named owns the file and install.sh does not
; overwrite it. Every name in it comes from a cluster's external-dns - static
; ones too, as a route through a proxy (core's proxmox.home, gatus.home).
$TTL 300
@        IN SOA  ns.home. hostmaster.home. ( 1 3600 600 86400 300 )
         IN NS   ns.home.
ns       IN A    192.168.8.1
